      "problem": "Which of the following gives the total area enclosed by graph of the polar curve $r=9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
